{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":59,"text":"After winning England in 1066, William the Conqueror wanted a fortress to show everyone who was in charge. Around 1078, he began the Great Square Keep in the middle, later whitewashed and named the White Tower. The kings who followed added walls, towers, and a moat full of water, and the castle became a palace, a treasury, a mint for making coins, and a prison for people the king thought were dangerous. It was even a zoo. In 1252, the king of Norway sent a polar bear, which was allowed to fish in the Thames on a long rope. Today, the crown jewels sparkle in a strong room. At least six ravens strut across the grass, because a legend says the kingdom will fall if they leave. And the guards in red and blue, the yeoman warders, nicknamed beefeaters, live inside the walls with their families. The moat was drained in 1843 and turned into a lawn. Every night for 700 years, the gates have been locked with the same ceremony.","words":[{"word":"After","start":0,"end":0.6399999856948853},{"word":"winning","start":0.6399999856948853,"end":0.9800000190734863},{"word":"England","start":0.9800000190734863,"end":1.3799999952316284},{"word":"in","start":1.3799999952316284,"end":1.7599999904632568},{"word":"1066","start":1.7599999904632568,"end":2.559999942779541},{"word":"William","start":3.299999952316284,"end":3.299999952316284},{"word":"the","start":3.299999952316284,"end":3.700000047683716},{"word":"Conqueror","start":3.700000047683716,"end":4.119999885559082},{"word":"wanted","start":4.119999885559082,"end":4.460000038146973},{"word":"a","start":4.460000038146973,"end":4.900000095367432},{"word":"fortress","start":4.900000095367432,"end":5.179999828338623},{"word":"to","start":5.179999828338623,"end":5.480000019073486},{"word":"show","start":5.480000019073486,"end":5.679999828338623},{"word":"everyone","start":5.679999828338623,"end":6.159999847412109},{"word":"who","start":6.159999847412109,"end":6.440000057220459